#2458
Entry into the Darkness~
A cold rush of air rushes up from the depths of the caverns, one that
could chill a frost giant.  The uncompromising, black granite walls
reflect the flickering light back in a thousand ways, making this
place seem surreal, almost otherwordly.  A steep slope heads east,
downward into darkness.  There are no sounds of movement or voices at
all, only the steady, quiet drip of the caverns' moist walls.
~
